.TH CHTTP_METHOD_STR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_method_str \- give the canonical string for an HTTP method
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

const char *chttp_method_str(chttp_method_t m);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function gives the uppercase ASCII method string for the enum
value that you give it, for example "GET" or "POST".  For CHTTP_ANY it
gives "ANY"; CHTTP_ANY is a sentinel for a route on the server
side and not a real HTTP method.  For an invalid value the function
falls back to "UNKNOWN".
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to a static string literal, which you must not free.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_request_new (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_method (3)
